## 🛠️ Compilation

The projects follow the compilation requirements of the 42 C++ modules.

Typical compilation:

```bash
c++ -Wall -Wextra -Werror -std=c++98
```

For example:

```bash
c++ -Wall -Wextra -Werror -std=c++98 main.cpp
```

Each exercise contains its own `Makefile` when required.

---

## 🎯 What I Learned

Across these five modules, I developed a foundation in modern programming concepts while working within the constraints of **C++98**.

The main progression was:

```text
C++ Basics
    ↓
Memory & References
    ↓
Operator Overloading
    ↓
Inheritance
    ↓
Polymorphism & Abstraction
```

These projects helped me understand not only how to use C++, but also how to design classes and structure larger programs using Object-Oriented Programming principles.

